I've written all five modules, but I can't tell whether the owner's answers will change them. I'm asking about the spec conflicts below and have coded each one in a conservative way.

<ask_owner>1) C11 says transfers "cost the sending side money per unit", but data.toml names the value `transfer_credit_cents_per_unit = 25`. Is it a debit from the sender (as the clause says) or a credit?
2) FILM has `shelf_life_days = 0`, but C13/C01 require perishables to have a shelf life of at least 1. Should `add_item` reject it, or does 0 mean non-perishable?
3) C18: what is the late-penalty percentage? (C23): are returned perishables restocked or discarded?
4) C16 `place_order` has no warehouse argument. May I add an optional `wh`?</ask_owner>

